mption"},{"text":"Energy prices where appropriate"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Moving averages"},{"text":"Exponential smoothing"},{"text":"Regression"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then progress to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ARIMA"},{"text":"Advanced time-series models"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Neural networks where justified"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 3–4 — Energy Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand how organizations manage energy strategically."},{"type":"h","text":"Energy Management Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Energy monitoring"},{"text":"Energy baselines"},{"text":"Performance indicators"},{"text":"Continuous improvement"},{"text":"Energy-saving programs"},{"text":"Energy management reporting"},{"text":"Understand the principles behind ISO 50001-style energy management systems."}]}]},{"heading":"Carbon & Sustainability Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern Energy Analysts increasingly work with carbon data."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scope 1 emissions"},{"text":"Scope 2 emissions"},{"text":"Scope 3 fundamentals"},{"text":"Emission factors"},{"text":"Carbon accounting"},{"text":"Renewable energy procurement"},{"text":"Energy transition"},{"text":"Decarbonization strategies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic Framework"},{"type":"flow","items":["Energy Consumption","Emission Factor","Carbon Emissions","Identify Major Sources","Reduction Opportunities","Track Progress"]}]},{"heading":"Grid & Power-System Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student does not necessarily need to become a power-system engineer, but should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electricity generation"},{"text":"Transmission"},{"text":"Distribution"},{"text":"Grid demand"},{"text":"Load curves"},{"text":"Grid balancing"},{"text":"Distributed generation"},{"text":"Net